# EnvironmentPostProcessor is still registered through spring.factories in Boot 3.x. Only
# auto-configuration moved to AutoConfiguration.imports, which is a different mechanism.
#
# This one refuses to start on an unsafe production configuration, before the application context
# exists and therefore before Flyway or the datasource can fail first with something less useful.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
ai.dival.dip.common.config.ProductionSafetyEnvironmentPostProcessor
